## Design on file for the record experiment

Draft of the design worker (2026-11-14), not reviewed: gate G0 is open. Abbreviations (EOC, FL, MEL, HYP) are explained at the top of [the catalogue](../../openwave-push/mf/T_designs/DESIGNS.md).

1. Hypothesis, not derived. "The proposed mass is the defect's excess rest energy over the reference, read in the
   same clock and energy dictionary that controls its propagation and interactions" (HYP 113-115). "The
   maintenance-to-energy map must be derived" (HYP 118). One identity exists on the coherent seam program: "⟨I − Re
   U⟩ = P(record 1) on every blank-record input with uniform address, so the energy clock reads read probabilities"
   (EOC 2389-2391).
2. X-MAINT on A: one excess unit above a balanced background of level h in {1, 2, 5}, on one carrier and on a cubic
   block of side 6. A defect observer (ports within one seam of the unit, co-moving through displacement records, FL
   1040-1042) and a reference observer with the same access far away hold the movement bits B = |j| of their
   incident attempts. Observable: ε = mean B (defect) − mean B (reference) per own tick. Description: an additive,
   background-independent rest rate; unit map U = 511 keV/ε. Gates: ε equal across h and sizes (exact arm 1e-12);
   two units at distance ≥ 2 give 2ε; kinetic gate: on D′ (choice register unread) the zero-momentum phase ω0 obeys
   1 − cos ω0 = ε within 1 %. Controls that fail: swap-always law (ε = 1); hold law (ε = 0).
3. Supplied: the 511 keV anchor (named by the criterion; one anchor is admitted, PC2 238); background; co-moving
